/*
class Node
{
    int data;
    Node left, right;

    Node(int item)
    {
        data = item;
        left = right = null;
    }
}
*/

class Tree {
    public ArrayList<Integer> reverseLevelOrder(Node root) {

        ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();                            // Initialize result list
        Queue<Node> q = new ArrayDeque<>();                                     // Queue for BFS traversal
        Deque<Integer> s = new ArrayDeque<>();                                  // Stack to reverse order
        
        q.add(root);                                                            // Enqueue root node
        
        while(!q.isEmpty()){                                                    // Process all nodes
            Node cur = q.remove();                                              // Dequeue current node
            s.push(cur.data);                                                   // Push current node value to stack
            
            if(cur.right != null){ q.add(cur.right); }                          // Enqueue right child first
            if(cur.left != null){ q.add(cur.left); }                            // Enqueue left child second
        }
        
        while(!s.isEmpty()){                                                    // Pop from stack to reverse
            list.add(s.pop());                                                  // Add popped value to result
        }   

        return list;                                                            // Return reverse level order
    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

Example: root = [10, 20, 30, 40, 60]

       10
      /  \
     20   30
    / \ 
   40  60

Queue: [10]
→ pop 10, stack=[10], add 30, 20
Queue: [30, 20]
→ pop 30, stack=[30,10], add nothing
Queue: [20]
→ pop 20, stack=[20,30,10], add 60, 40
Queue: [60, 40]
→ pop 60, stack=[60,20,30,10], add nothing
Queue: [40]
→ pop 40, stack=[40,60,20,30,10], add nothing
Queue: []

Pop stack: 40, 60, 20, 30, 10

Output: 40 60 20 30 10

//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Reverse Level Order Traversal
Given a binary tree, find its reverse level order traversal (start from the last level).

Examples:

----------------------------------------------------------------

Input: root = [1, 3, 2]
       1
     /   \
    3     2

Output: 3 2 1
Explanation: Level 1: 3 2, Level 0: 1

----------------------------------------------------------------

Input: root = [10, 20, 30, 40, 60]
       10
      /  \
     20   30
    / \ 
   40  60

Output: 40 60 20 30 10
Explanation: Level 2: 40 60, Level 1: 20 30, Level 0: 10

----------------------------------------------------------------

Input: root = [1, 2, 3]
       1
     /   \
    2     3

Output: 2 3 1

----------------------------------------------------------------

Constraints:
• 1 ≤ n ≤ 10^5

